WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.960
"The Witcher's" Yennefer of Vengerberg has&nbsp;
a brutal and generally unforgiving life.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.960
Originally cursed and ostracized by her&nbsp;
community for her elvish blood, Yennefer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.680
is further outcasted from society thanks to&nbsp;
being born with a hunchback and an awkward gait.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.480
Her family later sells her&nbsp;
to the passing mage Tissaia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.080
the headmistress of Aretuza,&nbsp;
an academy for female mages.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.360
Tissaia senses an untapped potential&nbsp;
in the brow-beaten Yennefer, though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.280
her new life at Aretuza is, at first,&nbsp;
little better than the one she had.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.600
Ambitious to a fault and craving great&nbsp;
power, Yennefer uses a combination of guile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.040
intimidation, and cunning in Season&nbsp;
1 to finally learn to use magic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.160
while at the same time transforming her visage to&nbsp;
become beautiful, though at great personal cost.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.000
Season 2 picks up after Yennefer taps&nbsp;
into the forbidden magic of fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.800
which saves the day and stops&nbsp;
the Nilfgaardian advance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.480
but leaves her bereft of the magic&nbsp;
that defines so much of her existence.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.960
Once again, Yennefer is put in a place where she&nbsp;
is willing to do anything to get her power back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.520
It all sets the stage for a&nbsp;
season 2 scene that had even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.440
the biggest Yennefer fans worried about&nbsp;
how the show is handling her character.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.320
The second episode of Season 2, "Kaer Morhen",&nbsp;
sees Yennefer, Fringilla, and Francesca invoke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.360
a supposedly ancient elvish deity. But when they&nbsp;
do, the apparition conjured whisks the three away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.360
and offers each of them their hearts' desire,&nbsp;
though it is implied there will be a cost.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.680
"If that's your play, it's rather desperate."

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.680
"You're the desperate one, Yennefer – the most."

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.160
Both Fringilla and Francesca agree,&nbsp;
but Yennefer initially refuses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.360
However, Yennefer is later captured&nbsp;
and about to be executed when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.720
invokes the litany that summons the&nbsp;
"Deathless Mother," who promises to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.720
return magic to Yennefer in exchange for&nbsp;
a young girl whom she doesn't recognize.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.000
Yennefer reluctantly agrees, and&nbsp;
the desperation in her eyes is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.480
palpable. This is a pretty big sacrifice that&nbsp;
would make even the evilest person wince,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.840
but Yennefer is willing to do&nbsp;
anything at this point in Season 2.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.880
She eventually comes across&nbsp;
her target. In a twist of fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.680
it turns out to be Geralt's adoptive child, Ciri.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.680
The Deathless Mother feeds off pain and&nbsp;
suffering, and, had Yennefer sacrificed Ciri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.880
there would have been tremendous&nbsp;
pain for both Geralt and herself.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.040
To a degree, Yennefer's actions shouldn't&nbsp;
come as too much of a surprise. In Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.760
audiences saw how Yennefer reacts to a world that&nbsp;
treats her with cruelty before she transforms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.520
After she changes, with the physical&nbsp;
traits society once shunned her for now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.560
fixed, she goes on to embrace her power as a&nbsp;
sorceress, using her magic for both good and ill.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.200
Yennefer's shocking turn, however brief,&nbsp;
left fans of "The Witcher" polarized.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.320
Her ability to toe the line between&nbsp;
hero and villain is intriguing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.120
and part of what makes her such a&nbsp;
complex and compelling character.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.840
It was this complex nature that had fans&nbsp;
reacting right and left on Reddit. Many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.640
expressed how upset they were with this scene and&nbsp;
its implications on her character arc in Season 2.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.160
On the subreddit r/netflixwitcher,&nbsp;
one Redditor wrote,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.440
"Really disappointed in Yen this season and&nbsp;
I thought she was one of the best characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.520
in season 1. I was really looking forward to&nbsp;
her teaching Ciri about magic [...] but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.760
storyline was basically compressed into two or&nbsp;
three scenes when they were riding to Cintra.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.840
Also did not like that Yen was planning&nbsp;
to sacrifice Ciri to get her powers back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.200
This really puts a weird strain on&nbsp;
their relationship from here on out."

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.120
Another user offered a rebuttal, saying,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.920
"But then Yen warned Ciri, and later sacrificed&nbsp;
herself for her. Plus Geralt loves her, meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.680
Yen is so impressed and enamored by&nbsp;
Ciri that all will be soon forgotten.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.560
It's hard to hate someone who&nbsp;
actively and obviously adores you."

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.000
A different poster acknowledged that the&nbsp;
show develops Yennefer and Ciri's dynamic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.160
differently than the way it develops in&nbsp;
Andrzej Sapkowski "The Witcher" books. There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.560
Yennefer has a more friendly, almost maternal&nbsp;
stance and helps Ciri learn about her magic.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.960
As we see in this particularly divisive Season&nbsp;
2 scene, Yennefer's actions lay the foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.800
for a different tone in her relationship&nbsp;
with Ciri. As the Reddit user wrote,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.080
"In the show, she doesn't know Ciri&nbsp;
and she's desperate to get her powers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.040
People make stupid decisions when they're&nbsp;
desperate so I get what they were trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.480
to do here. Would I have preferred&nbsp;
if they kept the book version? Yes."

